The label in E16 is "sd", so D16 should hold the standard deviation of the distribution in A11:A37 weighted by the counts in C11:C37. The mean is already in D15 and the total count is in H2 (D12 also sums the counts).

The weighted variance is SUMPRODUCT(C11:C37,(A11:A37-D15)^2)/H2, and its square root gives the standard deviation. This follows the same pattern as D15, which uses H2 as the divisor.

{"formula": "=SQRT(SUMPRODUCT(C11:C37,(A11:A37-D15)^2)/H2)"}

